course: dictionary
lesson: 14577
title: Pipework in everyday life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pipework is a noun. It means the pipes in a building, machine or system, all taken together. When you talk about the pipework, you mean the whole set of pipes, not just one pipe.
explain: Think of the pipes hidden behind the walls and under the floors of your home. They carry water, gas or hot water for heating. «The plumber checked the pipework under the kitchen sink.» Here pipework means all the pipes under that sink, working as one system.
explain: Engineers also talk about pipework in machines and factories. «The factory's pipework carried oil to every machine.» When you meet this word, ask yourself: are these pipes working together as one system? If so, pipework is the right word.
fact: Pipework means the pipes in a building, machine or system, taken all together.
fact: Pipework is uncountable, so do not use a or an with it: «Some pipework needs fixing.»
fact: Pipework can carry water, gas, oil or heating.
fact: Frozen pipework is a common winter problem, so pipes are often lagged, which means wrapped to keep them warm.
fact: A plumber is a person who fixes and installs pipework.
exercise: «The plumber checked the pipework under the sink.» What does pipework mean here? | *The pipes under the sink, taken all together | A cupboard with a door | A tool for cutting wood | The taps and the plug only
exercise: «Frozen pipework can be a problem in winter.» Why are pipes often lagged? | *To keep them warm | To stop them being seen | To make the water taste better | To make them bigger
exercise: Which meaning fits pipework best? | *The pipes in a building, machine or system | A person who fixes roofs | A machine that makes bread | A type of paint
test: «The factory's pipework carried oil to every machine.» What does pipework mean in this sentence? | *All the pipes in the factory system, taken together | The workers who built the factory | The oil itself | A single pipe that breaks easily
test: Which sentence uses pipework correctly? | The pipework are very cheap | I bought a pipework from the shop | Look at the pipeworks in the hall | *Some pipework needs fixing under the floor
exam: Which statement about pipework is true? | Pipework is countable, so you can say two pipeworks | Pipework is a kind of food | *Pipework means pipes taken all together, and it is uncountable | Pipework only carries gas
